    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3670" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρο-φύσιον</span></b> , τό,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῦσα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>snout</i> or <i>pipe of pair of bellows</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				992
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.100
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥήματα . . ἐπιδεικνύναι πάντ᾽
				ἀπ᾽ ἀκροφυσίων</span> fresh from <i>the bellows</i> (as
			we say, 'from the anvil'), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				699
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>comet's tail</i>, <i><span class="en">
